ChFi3d: a tight corner at a cylinder's rim (1590) is obtuse by the other
wall's normal where the corner's ball touches it, not where the wall meets
the face U (mitcad#2291, GitHub mitcad/Mitcad#592).

The case: a block 30 long, 10 high and 20 deep whose top meets a concave
quarter cylinder of radius 10 (a cut-out running down to the bottom), the
cylinder's axis lying in the top's plane. The end face's edge with the
cut-out is rounded with 2 (a torus K about the cut-out's axis), then the
end face's edge with the top with 3: the chain runs on round K's arc on
the top and along the top's edge with the cut-out. 1590's ChFi3d_TightArc
takes the arc (K a torus between the end face Wp and the cut-out Wo,
coaxial with it) and found the corner square: Wo's outward normal at its
line on the top is square to the top's. The acute corner was built: the
vertex blend's arc in the plane through the ball C parallel to the top,
the torus about Wo's rounding's axis turning it to K's meridian at e0
(Wo's normal at C's meridian), K cut there. But at C the cut-out's normal
e0 turns R / (rw + R) = 3 / 13 towards the top's normal: Wo's rounding
runs from the top's normal to e0, 13.3 degrees short of the direction
along the end face's rounding (ep) where the vertex blend's arc lies. Its
cylinder was carried on past its contact with Wo (a face of 0.0063 mm2),
and the torus ran from ep back to e0 over the part of K that is kept,
0.03 mm off it: the surface folded there, with a notch at each end of the
corner.

The condition: where Wo is a cylinder (KTorus), Obtuse is told by e0 as
PerformTightCorners finds it (C on the line R inside U and rw - sO R from
Wo's axis, sO +1 where Wo is convex): e0 . n = sO xU / (rw - sO R), xU the
height of C's line above Wo's axis along U's normal. Where Wo turns
towards U at C, the corner's own ball K rolls on between Wo and Wp's
rounding and then between the two roundings (1590's obtuse corner). At
the tube of 1590's case the two rules agree (the bore acute, -0.61; the
outside obtuse, +0.63); where C has no meridian (rw - sO R not above the
tolerance or below |xU|) the rule at Wo's line on U stays. Planar walls
(0970) are not changed: there e0 is Wo's normal.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2291.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
@@ -5644,6 +5644,19 @@ static bool ChFi3d_TightArc(const TopoDS_Edge&   Ek,
     }
     (aSqT ? D.nb : D.na) = no;
     D.Obtuse             = no.Dot(D.n) > angTol;
+    // (Obtuse by Wo's outward normal where the ball C touches it, e0 of
+    // PerformTightCorners, on the meridian of C, R inside U and R inside
+    // Wo: Wo's rounding runs from U's normal to e0, and the acute corner's
+    // vertex blend and torus need it to reach the direction along Wp's
+    // rounding. About a cylinder Wo, e0 is not Wo's normal at its line on
+    // U: where U holds K's axis, Wo is square to U along its line, but e0
+    // turns R / (rw + R) towards U's normal, mitcad#2291.)
+    const double xU   = gp_Vec(D.n).Dot(gp_Vec(D.CylO.Location(), PlU.Location())) - R;
+    const double rho0 = D.CylO.Radius() - sO * R;
+    if (rho0 > tol && rho0 * rho0 >= xU * xU)
+    {
+      D.Obtuse = sO * xU / rho0 > angTol;
+    }
   }
   else
   {
